From 2fe2c2016575212a823a43ed8e1b5ab72e3a7301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:45:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/45] Implant NeuraJL: real baseToolsFactory adapter, session
 persistence proven end to end

Closes NIRA_OPERATOR_SURFACE_STAGING.md's "prepares the chassis only" gap
with a real, working adapter -- not a stub, not a plan.

createNeurajlBaseToolsFactory (packages/coding-agent/src/core/tools/neurajl.ts)
uses baseToolsFactory, not the baseToolsOverride the staging doc originally
named -- deliberately: baseToolsFactory constructs tools once per agent
session (including once per RLM child) with a real dispose hook, exactly
the shape a persistent operator runtime needs. baseToolsOverride shares one
static tool map across every session that asks for it, which would mean
every session (and every RLM child) silently sharing ONE Julia kernel's
mutable bindings -- precisely the failure mode NeuraJL's own
C_child subset-of C_caller authority model exists to prevent one level
down. Reusing baseToolsOverride here would have reintroduced the same
problem at the chassis layer.

The tool spawns one persistent `security/session_cli.py` process (new in
ijulia-operator-lab) per agent session and drives it for that session's
whole lifetime via newline-JSON turns -- unlike neurabash.ts's own current
first pass, which is explicitly one-shot ("session persistence... is real
future work, not done here"). This is the actual point of NeuraJL's
architecture this whole pass: real state, real compiled methods, surviving
across separate tool calls.

Exported from the real public entry point (tools/index.ts -> sdk.ts),
alongside createNeurabashTool.

Proven through createAgentSession itself, not stubs
(test/suite/neurajl-substrate-modes.test.ts): state persisting across
SEPARATE tool calls, an ephemeral turn not leaking into the persistent
kernel AND not breaking the turn after it (the exact bug found and fixed
below), and dispose actually terminating the underlying process rather
than being a no-op.

A real, serious bug was found and fixed building the bridge -- in
ijulia-operator-lab (commit fc0f727), not in this fork: every
`subprocess.run(["julia", ...])` call there that didn't explicitly set
stdin= inherited the caller's own stdin, and `julia -e ...` (confirmed,
unlike e.g. /bin/true) silently breaks the caller's own subsequent reads
from it. Invisible in every prior one-shot caller; fatal for
session_cli.py, whose own broker runs in a background thread inside the
SAME process and calls exactly this code path for every ephemeral turn.
A model's first ephemeral: true call in a real chassis session would have
silently broken every turn after it.

Known, pre-existing, unrelated gap: this checkout's chassis-wide
`npm run build`/tsgo --noEmit fails because @earendil-works/pi-agent-core
and pi-ai have no built dist/ at all, breaking module resolution for
every file that imports them -- including the already-shipped
neurabash.ts. vitest (esbuild transpilation, not a full program
type-check) is unaffected and is what actually verified this work: full
`npm run test` sweep shows 95 pre-existing failures across unrelated
areas (daemon-supervisor, extensions-discovery, mcp-catalog,
model-registry, release-signatures), none touching
neurajl/neurabash/sdk.ts/tools/index.ts. Recorded in the staging doc so
it doesn't need rediscovering.

